---
---
<section id="how-it-works" class="border-t border-rule bg-ink px-6 py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div class="mb-16">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-sage-100 opacity-60">Sharing model</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-white sm:text-4xl">
        One URL. <em class="text-sage-100 opacity-80">Two modes.</em>
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-16 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1fr]">
      <!-- The URL breakdown -->
      <div>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-white opacity-70 max-w-md">
          Every board has a slug and an edit token. The token lives in the URL fragment — browsers never send fragments to the server. The client reads it and sends it only when saving.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-10 space-y-3">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-white opacity-40">Board URL</p>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-white/10 bg-white/5 px-5 py-4">
            <code class="font-mono text-sm text-white leading-relaxed whitespace-nowrap">
              <span class="opacity-40">https://your-server</span><span class="text-sage-100">/b/kitchen-board</span><span class="opacity-40">#</span><span class="text-clay-DEFAULT opacity-90">abcdef123456...</span>
            </code>
          </div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 pt-2">
            <div class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-4">
              <p class="font-mono text-xs text-sage-100 opacity-80">with #token</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-white opacity-60">Full edit access</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-4">
              <p class="font-mono text-xs text-white opacity-40">without fragment</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-white opacity-60">View only</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Steps -->
      <div class="space-y-0 divide-y divide-white/10">
        {[
          { n: '01', title: 'Create a board', body: 'Open the directory at /, give the board a name. A random slug is suggested. Create and get the full edit URL back.' },
          { n: '02', title: 'Bookmark the full URL', body: 'The URL with the #token is your edit link. Store it like a password — anyone who has it can change the board.' },
          { n: '03', title: 'Share a read-only link', body: 'Copy the same URL and remove everything from # onward. That link shows the board but disables all edits.' },
        ].map((step) => (
          <div class="py-7 flex gap-6">
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-white opacity-25 pt-1 flex-shrink-0 w-6">{step.n}</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">{step.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white opacity-55">{step.body}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}

        <div class="py-7">
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-white opacity-40">
            If you lose the edit token, recover it from <code class="font-mono text-white opacity-60">data/fridges/&lt;slug&gt;.json</code> on the host — look for the <code class="font-mono text-white opacity-60">"editToken"</code> field.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
